From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:44:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron): hold one-shots on uncheckable admission journals,
 naming the journal [daveey]

Follow-up to the three non-blocking review points on PR #1757 (review card t_01a1d1debe8ca7cc):

1. A malformed admission journal (bad JSON, missing/non-dict params, or a journal naming this
   job under the wrong key) still fails closed: the exhausted one-shot is kept and the journal
   is never deleted. The due scan now logs a warning naming the journal path instead of
   "Skipping malformed cron job <healthy job>".
2. claim_dispatch no longer lets a failed journal check escape to run_one_job's crash path
   (crash notice + mark_job_run(False) on an already-spent one-shot) in the concurrent
   exhaustion race: it holds the fire like any other pending-admission hold.
3. has_pending_admission and _sibling_pauses share one identity-checked journal iterator
   (_job_journals), so the identity rule lives in one place. Damaged journals raise
   CronJournalCorrupt (a ValueError carrying the path).

Tests: composed headless-tick test over five corrupt-journal shapes (job kept, journal kept,
journal named, healthy one-shot unaffected, legacy wedged cleanup resumes once the operator
removes the file) and a real run_one_job race test (no booking, no notice). RED on main:
6 failed (misleading "Skipping malformed cron job 'probe'" log; run_one_job returns False via
the crash path). GREEN: tests/cron 211 files, 1862 passed.
